# Outcome so-that

**Thesis:** A capability list is not an outcome until it says who benefits next. Every Core outcome statement needs `— so that <next entity> can <next capability>`, and the chain of so-thats must close back into the lattice.

Full law: `docs/build-foundation/08-outcome-so-that.md`  
Worked spine: `docs/register/OUTCOMES-TREE.md`

## Do

- Give every **Core** outcome a capability clause and a `so that` clause
- Name the **next entity already in the lattice** in the so-that (or register a new entity deliberately, in funnel order)
- Check the full chain of so-thats **closes** — the last one lands on an entity already named upstream
- Update the funnel comment in `outcomesRegistry.ts` when adding/reordering entities

## Don't

- Ship a Core statement that's just a capability list with no so-that
- Let a so-that dangle into infra/process language ("the system logs it", "the dashboard updates")
- Invent a so-that party that isn't an entity with its own outcomes
- Author a new entity's How graph when the task only asks for the registry `howGraphId` stub
